## Control {{controlId}}: Mark Media with Necessary CUI Markings and Distribution Limitations

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization marks media with CUI markings and distribution limitations within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through Microsoft Information Protection sensitivity labels and automated labeling rules managed by {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}.

{{#if dlpLabelsConfigured}}
**Automated CUI Marking:**
{{dlpLabelsCount}} sensitivity labels enforce CUI markings on digital media:
{{#each labels}}
- **{{name}}**{{#if isActive}} (Active){{else}} (Inactive){{/if}} — Priority: {{priority}}{{#if tooltip}} — {{tooltip}}{{/if}}
{{/each}}

Sensitivity labels apply:
- **Headers/Footers:** "CUI" or "CONTROLLED UNCLASSIFIED INFORMATION" markings on documents and emails
- **Watermarks:** Visual watermarks on CUI documents per 32 CFR Part 2002 requirements
- **Metadata:** Machine-readable classification tags embedded in file properties
- **Distribution Limitations:** "NOFORN," "FEDCON," or organization-specific dissemination controls applied via label policy
{{else}}
Sensitivity labels for CUI marking have not been configured. Media marking relies on manual procedures.
{{/if}}

**Paper Media Marking:**
Paper media containing CUI is marked with banner markings on each page per 32 CFR Part 2002, including CUI category, limited dissemination controls, and organization identifier.

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine sensitivity label configurations, header/footer/watermark settings, automated labeling rules, and paper media marking compliance samples.

